              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Strol 2E (UREVO store)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$169.99 against $289.99 “compare at” (28 Oct)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$161.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$8 less</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">SpaceWalk 3S (UREVO store)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$249.99 against $349.99 (every October check)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$239.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$10 less</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">CyberPad for Office (Amazon)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$431.99 (6 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$349.25</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$82.74 less</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            So the Black Friday cut on UREVO’s flat and 9% pads is about $10 against what they sold for in October, not the
            $100-plus the “compare at” price suggests. The CyberPad for Office on Amazon is the one with a real drop, and at
            $349.25 it is below the $389 our walking-pad deals page set as a target. We track the pads worth buying this
            week on our <a href="/cyber-monday-walking-pad-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday walking pad deals</a> page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="warranty-returns" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Warranty, Returns and Price Match: What UREVO Actually Promises</h2>
<p>
            UREVO’s warranty terms read differently depending on which of its pages you open, so it is worth knowing all
            three before you choose where to buy. On 27 November 2026:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[600px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">UREVO page</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What it says</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Store banner</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">“1-Year + 180-Day Extended Warranty”, “14-Day Hassle-Free Returns”, “30-Day Price Match Guarantee”</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Warranty policy</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">For purchases from official sellers (UREVO, Amazon, Walmart, eBay and other authorised retailers) on or after 20 March 2026, an extra 180 days after you download the UREVO app, bind the pad and register a 22–23 character serial number</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">FAQ</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Products bought on UREVO.com come with a 2-year warranty by default; other platforms default to 1 year; the 1-year + 180-day term needs registration in the app</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Return policy</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Returns within 14 days of receipt, unused, in original condition and packaging; you pay return shipping for a change of mind, UREVO pays for damaged, defective or wrong items</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The safe reading is one year, extended to 18 months if you bind the pad in UREVO’s app; the two-year figure in
            the FAQ is worth asking UREVO to confirm in writing if it decides where you buy. The 14-day, unused return
            window is short for a machine you can only judge by walking on it, and return shipping on a 40 to 70 lb pad is
            not trivial, so read our <a href="/treadmill-return-policies/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill return policies</a> guide and our <a href="/urevo-walking-pad-troubleshooting/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">UREVO walking pad troubleshooting</a> page before deciding a
            problem means a return.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="extras" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What UREVO Parts and Accessories Cost</h2>
<p>
            Budget pads fail in small ways first: a lost remote, a <a href="/treadmill-safety-key-not-working/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>lost safety key</a>, a dry belt. UREVO’s store priced the
            common parts on 27 November 2026:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Part or accessory</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">UREVO store (27 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Notes</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Replacement remote control</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$39.99–$49.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">UREVO’s FAQ says to send your model number so it can pair the right remote</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Safety key</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$9.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">UREVO says it will resend a weak or detached safety magnet</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Power cord</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$19.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sold out on 27 Nov</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walking pad handrail</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$59.99 (compare at $69.99)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Add-on for pads without a bar</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Foldable treadmill mat</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$39.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Floor protection and noise</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The remote is the part to think about. Many UREVO pads are controlled mainly by the remote or app, so a $40 to
            $50 replacement is a real cost if you lose it, and adding one to the price of a $150 pad changes the
            comparison with a pad that has buttons on the deck. Lubricant is the other running cost; UREVO’s Foldi 3S manual
            recommends 5 to 10 ml roughly every 100 miles, and our <a href="/how-to-lubricate-a-walking-pad/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">walking pad lubrication guide</a> covers how.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="which-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Which UREVO Is Worth the Money at Each Budget</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>About $150:</strong> the Strol 2E at $161.99 if you want a flat desk pad with a fold-up bar, or the
            Strol 2E Pro at $171.99 for a 12% manual incline and a 300 lb rating. For $10 more, the Pro is the better
            buy for most people.</li>
            <li><strong>About $250:</strong> the SpaceWalk 3S at $239.99 or SpaceWalk 5L at $269.99 for a 9% powered
            incline you can change while walking, which is what makes a pad useful once flat walking feels easy.</li>
            <li><strong>About $300:</strong> the FoldiMix 5L at $294.99 if you want a 400 lb rating and a laptop desk.</li>
            <li><strong>About $350 to $430:</strong> a CyberPad, with 14% incline, the steepest UREVO pad. The Office version
            at $349.25 on Amazon was the cheapest way into one on 27 November.</li>
            <li><strong>About $900:</strong> the CyberMega is a running treadmill, not a pad; compare it with <a href="/folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>folding
            treadmills</a> from Horizon and NordicTrack before buying.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If you are deciding between brands, our <a href="/best-walking-pads-with-incline/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best walking pads with incline</a> roundup compares UREVO’s incline pads with MERACH, WalkingPad and others, and our <a href="/best-walking-pads/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best walking pads</a> guide covers flat pads.
          </p>
          <p>
            Delivery adds little time or money to a UREVO. Its FAQ says parcels within the US arrive within 5 to 7
            working days once a tracking number is issued, and its return policy lets you cancel from the order status page
            within one hour of ordering; after that you email UREVO, and an order already processed for shipping cannot be
            cancelled. That matters on a sale weekend, when it is easy to order the wrong version of a similar-looking pad.
            Check the model name in your basket against the table above before you pay, and if you are buying as a gift,
            remember the 14-day return window starts when the parcel arrives, not when it is unwrapped.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="vs-rivals" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>UREVO vs WalkingPad, MERACH, Cybergoing and Sunny</h2>
<p>
            UREVO competes on price with the other Amazon pad brands. On 27 November 2026:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[600px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Pad</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price (source)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Key difference</th></tr></thead>
